.TH tkutemplate n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutemplate
.PP
Editor for document templates: place blocks on the page, edit their attributes and table columns, preview the result as a PDF. Built on \fBtkutils::tkulayoutcanvas\fR (placing), \fBtclutils::tulayout\fR (merging) and \fBtclutils::tuopen\fR (opening the preview). The preview uses \fBpdf4tcltemplate\fR from pdf4tcllib, which is loaded only when a preview is asked for.
.PP
A template is the dict \fBpdf4tcltemplate\fR draws:
.CS
paper a4  margin 20  size 10
theme {accent {0.15 0.30 0.20}}
blocks {
    address {x 20 y 50 w 85 size 11 list 1}
    items   {type table x 20 y 108 w 170 cols {{key pos title Pos w 12} {key text title Item}}}
    note    {x 20 y 0 w 170 gap 8}
}
.CE
.PP
\fBtkulayoutcanvas\fR knows only \fBx y w h show\fR. The editor gives it those, takes back what was dragged or typed there, and merges it with \fBtulayout::mergeLayout\fR (keys \fBx y w show\fR), so type, font size, text, columns and the rest are never lost. The \fBh\fR the canvas shows is an estimate from the type and the sample data; it is not written back.
.SS API
.CS
set te [::tkutils::tkutemplate::widget .te ?options?]
::tkutils::tkutemplate::getTemplate $te
::tkutils::tkutemplate::setTemplate $te $template
::tkutils::tkutemplate::setSample $te $data
::tkutils::tkutemplate::select $te $blockId
::tkutils::tkutemplate::addBlock $te $id ?type?          ;# text pairs table image rule
::tkutils::tkutemplate::deleteBlock $te $id
::tkutils::tkutemplate::moveBlock $te $id up|down
::tkutils::tkutemplate::setBlock $te $id key value ?key value ...?
::tkutils::tkutemplate::loadFile $te $file
::tkutils::tkutemplate::saveFile $te $file
::tkutils::tkutemplate::preview $te ?file?               ;# -> PDF file
.CE
.PP
\fBsetBlock\fR checks what it sets (numbers, booleans, \fBtype\fR, \fBpage\fR, \fBalign\fR, colour as a theme name or \fBr g b\fR) and raises \fB{TKUTILS TKUTEMPLATE VALUE}\fR otherwise. An empty value removes the attribute, except \fBtype\fR and \fBcols\fR. A block that becomes a table gets two columns, an image a height.
.PP
\fBmoveBlock\fR changes the order, which matters: a block with \fBy 0\fR follows the block before it.
.SS Options
.TS
l l l.
Option	Default	Meaning
\fB\-template\fR	\fB{blocks {}}\fR	the template to edit
\fB\-sample\fR	\fB{}\fR	data for the preview, keyed like the data of \fBpdf4tcltemplate\fR
\fB\-onchange\fR	\fB{}\fR	\fBcmd $path $template\fR after every change
\fB\-scale\fR	\fB2.5\fR	pixels per mm on the canvas
\fB\-gridmm\fR	\fB5\fR	snap grid in mm
\fB\-font\fR / \fB\-fontbold\fR	\fB{}\fR	fonts for the preview; default: pdf4tcllib's TrueType faces
\fB\-width\fR / \fB\-height\fR	\fB560\fR / \fB640\fR	canvas size
.TE
.SS "The window"
.IP \(bu
Toolbar: \fBAdd block\fR (by type), \fBDelete\fR, \fBUp\fR, \fBDown\fR, \fBLoad…\fR, \fBSave…\fR, \fBPreview\fR.
.IP \(bu
Left: the page (\fBtkulayoutcanvas\fR) with the block list, x/y/w and visibility.
.IP \(bu
Right, three tabs:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu
\fBBlock\fR \-\- id (Return renames), type, size, bold, colour, align, leading, gap, page, field, list, labelw, h, zebra, text. A field is taken on Return or when it loses the focus; a bad value rings, shows the message under the editor and is undone.
.IP \(bu
\fBColumns\fR \-\- the columns of a table block: key, title, w, align; add, delete, up, down.
.IP \(bu
\fBPage\fR \-\- paper, margin, top, bottom, font size, the colours \fBaccent\fR and \fBmuted\fR.
.RE
.SS Preview
.PP
\fBpreview\fR draws the template with \fB\-sample\fR into a PDF and returns the file (a temp file when none is given); the button opens it with the system viewer. A block without sample data shows a stand\-in \-\- its id, a label/value pair, three table rows with the column keys \-\- so every block is visible. Without pdf4tcllib or without pdf4tcl the editor works, and \fBpreview\fR raises \fB{TKUTILS TKUTEMPLATE PREVIEW}\fR \-\- also when something goes wrong while drawing; a temp file it made is removed again.
.SS Files
.PP
\fBsaveFile\fR writes the template as Tcl, one block per line, so it reads well in an editor and in a diff. \fBloadFile\fR reads it back; the result equals the saved template.
.SS Launcher
.CS
wish bin/tkutemplate.tcl ?template.tcl?
.CE
.SS Demo
.CS
wish examples/demo-tkutemplate.tcl
.CE
.SS Tests
.CS
xvfb-run -a tclsh tests/tkutemplate.test
.CE
.PP
The preview tests need pdf4tcllib (sibling checkout or \fBPDF4TCLLIB_TM\fR) and pdf4tcl (\fBTCLLIBPATH\fR), one of them \fBpdftotext\fR; without them they are skipped. With pdf4tcllib but without pdf4tcl, a test checks that \fBpreview\fR reports \fB{TKUTILS TKUTEMPLATE PREVIEW}\fR.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB{TKUTILS TKUTEMPLATE OPTION|EXISTS|NOWIDGET|BLOCK|VALUE|FILE|PREVIEW}\fR
